# Copy to .env.local (ignored by Git) and fill in. These are the ONLY variables the application reads, and both
# are PUBLIC: they end up in the JavaScript every visitor downloads. What protects the data is Row Level
# Security in the database, not the secrecy of these values.
#
# NEVER put a secret key here (the "service_role" key or a key starting with "sb_secret_"): it bypasses Row
# Level Security. The application refuses to start with one.
#
# Leave both empty (or do not create the file) for the demonstration build: fictional data kept in the browser,
# no sign-in. Set both for the build with accounts.
#
# Local stack (`supabase start`, then `supabase status`): the API URL is http://127.0.0.1:54321 and the public key
# is the "Publishable" key (or the legacy "anon" key).
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
